WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.463 --> 00:00:18.304
the buildings in the dreary town of Mudfog was a workhouse, where the poor were housed and many

2
00:00:18.344 --> 00:00:19.605
of them were worked to death.

3
00:00:20.665 --> 00:00:25.546
Oliver Twist was born in this dismal place, but for a few minutes it was doubtful he would

4
00:00:25.566 --> 00:00:30.388
survive. At last he breathed, sneezed, and let out a loud wail.

5
00:00:31.360 --> 00:00:34.621
Hearing this, a young woman raised her head feebly from her pillow.

6
00:00:34.641 --> 00:00:37.822
"Let me see the child and die."

7
00:00:37.842 --> 00:00:42.823
"Oh, you must not talk about dying yet," said the doctor who had attended the birth.

8
00:00:43.824 --> 00:00:48.025
"Bless her heart, no," said the old pauper woman who was serving as nurse.

9
00:00:49.125 --> 00:00:51.666
"Think about being a mother to your new baby, dear."

10
00:00:52.566 --> 00:00:55.047
The young mother stretched out her hand toward the child.

11
00:00:55.987 --> 00:00:58.168
The doctor deposited the baby in her arms.

12
00:00:59.272 --> 00:01:03.756
She imprinted her cold lips passionately on his forehead, shuddered, and died.

13
00:01:03.776 --> 00:01:06.958
"It's all over," said the doctor.

14
00:01:06.979 --> 00:01:09.000
"She was a nice-looking girl.

15
00:01:09.821 --> 00:01:10.702
Where did she come from?"

16
00:01:10.722 --> 00:01:14.605
"She was brought here last night," replied the old woman.

17
00:01:15.626 --> 00:01:17.267
"She was found lying in the street.

18
00:01:18.208 --> 00:01:21.931
But where she came from or where she was going, nobody knows."

19
00:01:22.972 --> 00:01:24.413
The doctor leaned over the body.

20
00:01:24.433 --> 00:01:26.455
"The same old story."

21
00:01:27.335 --> 00:01:27.996
He shook his head.

22
00:01:28.976 --> 00:01:29.776
"No wedding ring.

23
00:01:30.617 --> 00:01:31.697
Well, good night.

24
00:01:32.758 --> 00:01:34.839
If the child cries, give it a little gruel."

25
00:01:35.739 --> 00:01:38.900
Wrapped in an old calico blanket, Oliver cried lustily.

26
00:01:39.921 --> 00:01:43.522
If he had known he was a workhouse orphan, he would have cried even louder.

27
00:01:44.443 --> 00:01:49.705
When Oliver was about eight months old, he was sent to a branch workhouse—a farm run by an

28
00:01:49.825 --> 00:01:50.445
elderly woman.

29
00:01:51.405 --> 00:01:54.207
Mrs. Mann was a woman of wisdom and experience.

30
00:01:55.287 --> 00:01:58.861
She knew what was good for the children under her care, and she knew what was good for

31
00:01:58.921 --> 00:02:04.686
her. So she took the greater part of their weekly stipends for her own use and fed the

32
00:02:04.746 --> 00:02:06.427
children as little as possible.

33
00:02:07.348 --> 00:02:12.352
By his tenth birthday, Oliver was a pale child, small for his age and quite thin.

34
00:02:13.332 --> 00:02:17.075
But luckily nature had planted a good, sturdy spirit in Oliver's heart.

35
00:02:17.996 --> 00:02:22.439
For he was spending his birthday locked in the coal cellar with two other orphans for daring to

36
00:02:22.459 --> 00:02:22.960
be hungry.

37
00:02:23.944 --> 00:02:28.127
Mrs. Mann looked out the window and saw a large, fat man fumbling with the latch on the

38
00:02:28.167 --> 00:02:28.687
front gate.

39
00:02:28.707 --> 00:02:31.129
"The parish officer is here!"

40
00:02:31.509 --> 00:02:32.550
she cried to her servant.

41
00:02:32.570 --> 00:02:37.153
"Take Oliver and those two brats upstairs and wash them right away before Mr.

42
00:02:37.233 --> 00:02:38.094
Bumble sees them!"

43
00:02:38.114 --> 00:02:40.415
"Why is this gate locked?"

44
00:02:40.815 --> 00:02:42.296
The man rattled the gate as Mrs.

45
00:02:42.356 --> 00:02:43.017
Mann appeared.

46
00:02:43.037 --> 00:02:45.679
"You're keeping a parish officer waiting.

47
00:02:46.579 --> 00:02:48.160
And I am here on official business!"

48
00:02:48.180 --> 00:02:51.443
"How delightful to see you, Mr.

49
00:02:51.463 --> 00:02:52.403
Bumble!" Mrs.

50
00:02:52.443 --> 00:02:53.344
Mann opened the gate.

51
00:02:54.324 --> 00:02:58.168
"I was just telling the dear children, who are so fond of you, that you're here."

52
00:02:59.068 --> 00:03:03.212
Mrs. Mann ushered him into the parlor, where he removed his hat, and they sat down.

53
00:03:03.232 --> 00:03:06.735
"Oliver Twist is ten years old today," said Mr.

54
00:03:06.755 --> 00:03:09.798
Bumble. "Bless him," interrupted Mrs.

55
00:03:09.858 --> 00:03:17.284
Mann. "And despite offering a reward of ten pounds—later increased to twenty pounds—the parish has never been able

56
00:03:17.324 --> 00:03:19.086
to discover the names of his parents."

57
00:03:20.047 --> 00:03:21.408
"Then how did he get a name?"

58
00:03:22.368 --> 00:03:24.349
Mr. Bumble drew himself up with pride.

59
00:03:24.369 --> 00:03:27.550
"I name all the orphans in alphabetical order.

60
00:03:28.431 --> 00:03:31.692
The last was Swubble, then Twist, then Unwin.

61
00:03:32.592 --> 00:03:35.914
But returning to business, Oliver is too old to remain here.

62
00:03:37.594 --> 00:03:41.276
I've come myself to take him back to the workhouse, so let me see him at once."

63
00:03:42.356 --> 00:03:43.837
Mrs. Mann went to fetch Oliver.

64
00:03:43.857 --> 00:03:47.779
"Make a bow to the gentleman, Oliver," she said when they returned.

65
00:03:48.739 --> 00:03:49.339
Oliver bowed.

66
00:03:49.359 --> 00:03:51.040
"Very good, Oliver.

67
00:03:52.020 --> 00:03:53.001
Now come along with me."

68
00:03:54.021 --> 00:03:55.242
And with that, Mr.

69
00:03:55.282 --> 00:03:57.944
Bumble put on his hat and bade the surprised Mrs.

70
00:03:57.984 --> 00:03:58.804
Mann good day.

71
00:03:59.845 --> 00:04:03.687
Mr. Bumble walked quickly down the road with little Oliver clutching his coat cuff.

72
00:04:04.667 --> 00:04:05.568
"Are we nearly there?"

73
00:04:05.968 --> 00:04:07.589
Oliver gasped every quarter mile.

74
00:04:07.609 --> 00:04:09.710
"Not yet," Mr.

75
00:04:09.730 --> 00:04:11.391
Bumble said with growing impatience.

76
00:04:12.472 --> 00:04:15.294
At last they arrived at a huge, prison-like building.

77
00:04:15.314 --> 00:04:18.816
"You've come here to be taught a useful trade," said Mr.

78
00:04:18.856 --> 00:04:25.517
Bumble. "Starting tomorrow morning at six o'clock, you'll pick apart old ropes so they can be reused."

79
00:04:26.538 --> 00:04:31.099
Oliver barely had time to look around before he was hurried away to receive his dreary uniform.

80
00:04:32.059 --> 00:04:36.380
That night he sobbed himself to sleep on a hard bed in a room full of other boys.

81
00:04:37.441 --> 00:04:38.561
Three months passed.

82
00:04:39.461 --> 00:04:44.223
The board running the workhouse decided that too many poor people were taking advantage of its services.

83
00:04:45.203 --> 00:04:49.044
To reduce the number of paupers, they drastically reduced the amount of food.

84
00:04:50.096 --> 00:04:53.318
Now each boy was allowed only one small bowl of gruel.

85
00:04:54.278 --> 00:04:56.220
The boys were fed in a great stone hall.

86
00:04:57.220 --> 00:05:01.883
Once a day, the master of the workhouse, assisted by two women, ladled out the gruel from a

87
00:05:01.943 --> 00:05:02.983
large copper pot.

88
00:05:03.003 --> 00:05:08.026
"If I don't get more to eat," said a new boy, "I might have to eat one of

89
00:05:08.086 --> 00:05:13.729
you." He glared at the other boys with a wild, hungry look in his eyes, frightening them.

90
00:05:14.810 --> 00:05:18.592
That night the boys decided that someone had to ask the master for more food.

91
00:05:19.584 --> 00:05:22.005
They drew lots, and Oliver got the job.

92
00:05:23.006 --> 00:05:25.507
The next evening the boys arrived in the dining hall.

93
00:05:26.508 --> 00:05:28.969
They stood in line while the master filled their bowls.

94
00:05:30.030 --> 00:05:32.811
Then they sat down, and the gruel quickly disappeared.

95
00:05:33.752 --> 00:05:36.213
The boys whispered to each other and winked at Oliver.

96
00:05:37.154 --> 00:05:39.815
Oliver was desperate with hunger and reckless with misery.

97
00:05:40.776 --> 00:05:43.317
He rose from the table and walked toward the master.

98
00:05:43.337 --> 00:05:44.798
"Please, sir."

99
00:05:45.178 --> 00:05:46.199
Oliver held up his bowl.

100
00:05:46.219 --> 00:05:48.220
"I want some more."

101
00:05:49.132 --> 00:05:51.913
The master aimed a blow at Oliver's head with his ladle.

102
00:05:52.813 --> 00:05:53.393
"Call Mr.

103
00:05:53.453 --> 00:05:59.735
Bumble!" The parish officer came running from a board meeting, and when he heard Oliver's request, he ran

104
00:05:59.855 --> 00:06:00.395
right back.

105
00:06:02.116 --> 00:06:03.016
"I beg your pardon, Mr.

106
00:06:03.036 --> 00:06:04.116
Limbkins," Mr.

107
00:06:04.136 --> 00:06:05.497
Bumble said to the head of the board.

108
00:06:06.437 --> 00:06:08.297
"Oliver Twist has asked for more food."

109
00:06:09.278 --> 00:06:11.338
There was horror on every face in the room.

110
00:06:11.358 --> 00:06:13.239
"For more?"

111
00:06:13.639 --> 00:06:14.079
said Mr.

112
00:06:14.119 --> 00:06:17.460
Limbkins. "Compose yourself, Bumble, and answer me.

113
00:06:18.444 --> 00:06:23.127
Do I understand he asked for more after he'd eaten the amount allotted to him?"

114
00:06:23.147 --> 00:06:25.709
"He did, sir," replied Mr.

115
00:06:25.749 --> 00:06:28.991
Bumble. "That boy will come to a bad end."

116
00:06:29.951 --> 00:06:32.713
Mr. Limbkins shook his head, and no one disagreed.

117
00:06:33.713 --> 00:06:35.234
Oliver was instantly locked up.

118
00:06:36.195 --> 00:06:41.638
The next morning a notice was posted on the workhouse gate, offering five pounds to anyone who wanted

119
00:06:41.718 --> 00:06:42.339
an apprentice.

120
00:06:43.419 --> 00:06:48.239
In other words, they were looking for anyone who would take Oliver Twist off the hands of the

121
00:06:48.279 --> 00:06:48.740
parish.
